# Misty Salon's "X is the number of unlocked doors among Rooms you control" (CR 709.5c): a Room counts each door unlocked, not
# the whole card. Turn 1, Bot1 casts one Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon as Smoky Lounge with Black Lotus's {R}{R}{R}; its Misty
# Salon door stays locked and is not counted. On turn 3 the {R}{R} it adds (spendable on a Room spell, `Spend: R, R, U, U`)
# and two Mox Sapphires pay the second copy cast as Misty Salon ({3}{U}), which unlocks as it enters (CR 709.5h): the
# trigger counts the first Room's one door and this one's, so a 2/2 blue flying Spirit, not a 3/3 (a Room's both halves) nor a 1/1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon
Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Island
Island
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon.Cast(Ability: Smoky Lounge)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = {R}{R} (RoomSpellsOrUnlockingDoors)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Smoky Lounge // Misty Salon.Cast(Ability: Misty Salon; Spend: R, R, U, U)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Battlefield.Smoky Lounge.Doors = Smoky Lounge
Bot1.Battlefield.Misty Salon.Doors = Misty Salon
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Spirit Token.Toughness = 2
